agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018YJzrfYJig1ZfY7x1dTjWK", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52244, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018YJzrfYJig1ZfY7x1dTjWK", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52244, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018YJzrfYJig1ZfY7x1dTjWK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 54679, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.002, down from 0.18).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release in production. v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy, so I rolled back to it. No new version was deployed, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the service mixed across versions. I retried the same rollback, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** The create-incident call timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and contains the full summary, including the partial failure and retry. It was created once.\n\nFollow-up for the on-call team: find out why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator partial failure, and decide when v2.3.1 can be re-released.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BVFrJMxJg3xRkYq2Xvx3xP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014Hs3PVVUC6xQwCSwsPNn8e", "caller": {"type": "di